@package Network
The `Network` package provides the abstractions and transports used to build
networked applications in Mint.

It is organized around three main layers:

* The {Network.Endpoint} abstraction describes peer addresses and the
  protocol-specific information needed to reach them.
* The {Network.Socket} abstraction represents a transport endpoint for a
  specific protocol family such as TCP or UDP.
* The {Network.Channel} and {Network.EventChannel} classes expose message-based
  communication over a socket. The synchronous channel is appropriate for
  direct use, while the event channel integrates with the runtime scheduler for
  asynchronous I/O.

The package also provides protocol-specific client and server classes for layers
5 to 7 of the OSI model, together with polling and runtime integration helpers.

```mn
load network.poller
load network.sockets.tcp
load network.endpoints.ip
load network.protocols.http.client

if let client = Network.Http.Client(Network.TcpSocket()) {
    client.onMessage = def (self, channel) {
        sendToBrowser(self.read())
    }

    client.connect(Network.IpEndpoint(serverHost, serverPort))

    let poller = Network.Poller()
    poller.watch(client)
    while running {
        poller.poll()
    }

    client.close()
}
```
